<title>JAPAN: Japan cartel to drill for oil in Azerbaijan.</title>
<headline>Japan cartel to drill for oil in Azerbaijan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A cartel of Japanese oil companies will sign an agreement next year to develop oil fields in Azerbaijan, a major Japanese business daily reported on Sunday.</p>
<p>The Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported that a consortium headed by Itochu Corp, Japan Energy Corp and Teikoku Oil Co Ltd have reached agreement with the Azerbaijan government on signing a deal in February allowing the companies to prospect for estimated reserves of 7.0 billion barrels in the southern Caspian Sea.</p>
</text>
